    "---\n",
    "## Section 2 — Concept Notes\n",
    "\n",
    "### What Is A/B Testing?\n",
    "An A/B test is a **controlled experiment** that compares two variants (A = control, B = treatment) on one or more metrics. It answers: *\"Is the observed difference real, or just random noise?\"*\n",
    "\n",
    "### Core Framework\n",
    "| Step | Action |\n",
    "|------|--------|\n",
    "| 1. Hypotheses | H₀: no difference; H₁: treatment changes the metric |\n",
    "| 2. Alpha (α) | Risk of false positive — industry standard: **0.05** |\n",
    "| 3. Power (1-β) | Probability of detecting a real effect — target: **0.80** |\n",
    "| 4. Run the test | Collect data for sufficient duration |\n",
    "| 5. Compute stat | z-test (proportions) or t-test (continuous) |\n",
    "| 6. Decision | p < α → reject H₀; p ≥ α → fail to reject H₀ |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Which Test for Which Metric?\n",
    "| Metric Type | Example | Test |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| Binary (0/1) | Conversion rate, click-through | **Two-proportion z-test** |\n",
    "| Continuous | AOV, session time, revenue | **Two-sample t-test (Welch)** |\n",
    "\n",
    "### Effect Size — Why p-value Alone Is Not Enough\n",
    "- **Cohen's d** (continuous): 0.2 = small, 0.5 = medium, 0.8 = large\n",
    "- **Cohen's h** (proportions): same scale\n",
    "- p < 0.05 only tells you *significance*, not *magnitude*.  \n",
    "  A tiny effect can be significant with a huge n. Always report both.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Multiple Testing Problem\n",
    "Testing 3 metrics simultaneously inflates false-positive risk from 5% to ~14%.  \n",
    "**Bonferroni correction:** adjust α threshold = 0.05 / number_of_tests\n",
    "\n",
    "### Power Analysis\n",
    "Tells you: *\"How many users do I need per group to detect an effect of this size?\"*  \n",
    "Running the test with too few users = **underpowered** → you might miss a real effect.\n",
    "\n",
    "### NRA Rule (Every Written Insight)\n",
    "> **Number + Reason + Action**  \n",
    "> ❌ \"Group B had higher AOV.\"  \n",
    "> ✅ \"Group B AOV of ₹1,569 is ₹124 higher than Group A (p=0.006, d=0.32), driven by the reduced friction in express checkout. Launch express checkout to all users to capture this revenue uplift immediately.\"\n"
